## 8. Open items

### 8.1 Multi-season priors — not yet tested
Every prediction currently uses **one** prior season. Combining 2-3 prior seasons
would give a steadier, less noisy prior (more minutes, more shots). Likely helps
most for the heavily-shrunk group (defenders). High-value next test.

### 8.2 True positions (RW/ST/CAM/CDM…) — deferred enrichment
FPL's four buckets lump a CDM and a CAM together as "MID" despite very different
scoring profiles. Finer positions (from FBref/Understat) would give more meaningful
priors. Deferred: it is a data-join project (naming mismatches, new signings), and
should be tested for actual lift before committing.

### 8.3 Finishing skill — the signal that genuinely beats xG
Shrinkage cleans xG but cannot exceed it. The real value-add *over* xG is
**finishing** — players who consistently score above their xG. That is a separate,
persistent signal worth modelling in the points layer (§3.4). Not built here.

### 8.4 Extend to other stats
Only npxG validated so far. xA (for creativity) and the goals/assists count
versions want the same per-position signal-to-noise treatment. For lumpy counts on
low minutes, the Poisson-count noise (§3.1) is appropriate and shrinkage should
genuinely help — the opposite regime from full-season npxG.

### 8.5 Final k confirmed on 8 seasons + held-out test — RESOLVED
The 2-season tuned k's were tested on 8 season-pairs and via an early→late held-out
split (§4.6). Verdict: per-cell tuning is false precision. **Final rule: FWD npxG
k=2, everything else k=10.** Only remaining step is one confirmation pass on the
sealed 2025-26 test at the very end (not yet done — do not tune against it).

