## 9. Summary

| finding | result |
|---|---|
| Shrinkage's role | noise-cleanup step, not a prediction model; feeds the points model |
| Correct noise for goals | Poisson-count formula (variance = mean) |
| Correct noise for xG | must be **measured** (split-half); count formula overestimates 5× |
| Noise must be **per-position** | FWD 0.0195, MID 0.0059, DEF 0.0016 — pooling breaks defenders |
| Per-cell k tuning | **false precision** — 8-season + held-out early/late test showed no reliable out-of-sample gain |
| **Final k** | **FWD npxG = 2; everything else (npxG MID/DEF, all xA) = 10** |
| xA finding | DEF predicts xA *best* (0.71) — set-piece/cross roles are repeatable & stable |
| Finishing (goals−xG) | weak/non-persistent (FWD 0.19, MID/DEF noise); NOT price-related; not used |
| Shot volume | real out-of-sample signal for **DEF** (+0.081); minor for MID; skip FWD |
| The principle | shrink noisy rates, trust clean ones — but estimate strength only at a resolution the data supports |
| Bug #6 | `element` reshuffles across seasons; use Understat `id`; old 0.30→0.43 invalid |
| Price-tier priors | tested, redundant with npxG (price still valuable for minutes) |

**2025-26 test season remains untouched.**